---
description: Git commits must not include co-author or contributor trailers
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git commits — author only

When creating or amending git commits:

- **Never** add `Co-authored-by`, `Signed-off-by`, `Reviewed-by`, or similar contributor trailers to the commit message.
- The commit message must contain only the subject and optional body (no attribution trailers).
- Use only the repository author's identity from local git config (`user.name`, `user.email`).
- Do not pass `--trailer` or any flag that adds co-authors or extra contributors.
- Do not append Cursor, AI, or bot attribution lines to commit messages.
